{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/maxDistance"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"externalID":"s:10SwiftGodot15ReflectionProbeC11maxDistanceSdvp","symbolKind":"property","role":"symbol","title":"maxDistance","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxDistance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"}]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"final"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maxDistance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"set"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The maximum reflection distance is always at least equal to the probe’s extents. This means that decreasing ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/maxDistance","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" will not always cull objects from reflections, especially if the reflection probe’s box defined by its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/size","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is already large.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The maximum distance away from the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" an object can be before it is culled. Decrease this to improve performance, especially when using the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/UpdateMode-swift.enum\/always","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/updateMode-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/reflectionprobe\/maxdistance"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/ReflectionProbe/UpdateMode-swift.enum/always":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"always"}],"title":"ReflectionProbe.UpdateMode.always","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/reflectionprobe\/updatemode-swift.enum\/always","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Update the probe every frame. This provides better results for fast-moving dynamic objects (such as cars). However, it has a significant performance cost. Due to the cost, it’s recommended to only use one ReflectionProbe with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/UpdateMode-swift.enum\/always","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" at most per scene. For all other use cases, use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/UpdateMode-swift.enum\/once","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/UpdateMode-swift.enum\/always"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/ReflectionProbe":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ReflectionProbe","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ReflectionProbe","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/reflectionprobe","title":"ReflectionProbe","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Captures its surroundings to create fast, accurate reflections from a given point."}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/ReflectionProbe/UpdateMode-swift.enum/once":{"title":"ReflectionProbe.UpdateMode.once","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/UpdateMode-swift.enum\/once","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/reflectionprobe\/updatemode-swift.enum\/once","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Update the probe once on the next frame (recommended for most objects). The corresponding radiance map will be generated over the following six frames. This takes more time to update than "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/UpdateMode-swift.enum\/always","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", but it has a lower performance cost and can result in higher-quality reflections. The ReflectionProbe is updated when its transform changes, but not when nearby geometry changes. You can force a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" update by moving the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" slightly in any direction."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"once"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/ReflectionProbe/maxDistance":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/maxDistance","title":"maxDistance","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxDistance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/reflectionprobe\/maxdistance","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The maximum distance away from the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe"},{"type":"text","text":" an object can be before it is culled. Decrease this to improve performance, especially when using the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/UpdateMode-swift.enum\/always"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/updateMode-swift.property"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/ReflectionProbe/updateMode-swift.property":{"title":"updateMode","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/updateMode-swift.property","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/reflectionprobe\/updatemode-swift.property","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sets how frequently the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is updated. Can be "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/UpdateMode-swift.enum\/once","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/UpdateMode-swift.enum\/always","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"updateMode"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ReflectionProbe","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot15ReflectionProbeC"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UpdateMode","preciseIdentifier":"s:10SwiftGodot15ReflectionProbeC10UpdateModeO"}]},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/ReflectionProbe/size":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ReflectionProbe\/size","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"size"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:17SwiftGodotRuntime7Vector3V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vector3"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/reflectionprobe\/size","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The size of the reflection probe. The larger the size, the more space covered by the probe, which will lower the perceived resolution. It is best to keep the size only as large as you need it."}],"title":"size"}}}